        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "An exceptional Tudor-style country residence set on approximately 0.6 acres of mature, beautifully landscaped grounds, offering an impressive combination of traditional character, refined craftsmanship and contemporary luxury.\n\nExtending to approximately 285 square metres, the property makes a striking impression from the moment of arrival, with a gated entrance, mature planting to the front and an attractive country-house façade complemented by high-end terracotta roof tiles. The sense of quality continues throughout the home, with a particularly impressive staircase forming a beautiful centrepiece to the accommodation.\n\nOne of the property`s most notable features is the exceptional flow between the principal living spaces. The bespoke French Oak kitchen forms the heart of the home and is complemented by a large dining room, creating an ideal environment for everyday family life and relaxed entertaining. The kitchen is beautifully appointed with a Belfast sink and benefits from an additional spacious walk in room that can be used as a pantry. Off the kitchen, a generous utility room, a downstairs WC and a charming half-door to the rear of the property add practicality and convenience.\n\nThe accommodation continues with a large living room plus a versatile multi-function lounge with fireplaces, offering flexibility for relaxation, informal entertaining or family use. The timber doors are fitted with antique Suffolk locks and hinges, adding a distinctive touch of traditional character to the living space. A delightful sun room provides an additional space from which to enjoy the surrounding gardens and countryside, while a dedicated home office offers an ideal environment for working from home.\n\nUpstairs, the sense of luxury continues with four generously proportioned double bedrooms, each enjoying its own impressive view. Two of the bedrooms benefit from private en-suite facilities, while the principal bathroom features a beautiful free-standing bath, creating a tranquil and elegant space in which to unwind.\n\nExternally, the property enjoys generous private grounds, with mature planting creating an established and attractive setting to the front. To the rear, a patio area provides an excellent space for outdoor entertaining, while the view across expansive green fields creates a wonderful sense of space and tranquillity.\nCompleting the property is a substantial extra-large garage, offering excellent storage and practical utility space.\n\nThe location is particularly appealing, offering an excellent balance of countryside, coast and connectivity. Gorey and Arklow are both approximately 15 minutes away, while Dublin can be reached in under an hour. The beach is also just five minutes from the property, providing easy access to the coast. Subject to confirmation, school bus services for both primary and secondary education may also be available from outside the property entrance.\n\nA rare opportunity to acquire a beautifully presented, high-end country residence extending to approximately 285 square metres, in a central and highly convenient location close to local towns, beautiful beaches and within easy reach of Dublin. Exceptional craftsmanship, elegant interiors, four impressive double bedrooms and a peaceful countryside setting combine to create a truly special home.\n"
      },
